A Terraform Module is a collection of Terraform configuration files grouped together to create and manage infrastructure in a reusable way.

Instead of writing the same Terraform code repeatedly, you can create a module once and reuse it across multiple projects.

1. Why Do We Use Terraform Modules?
========================================
Reusability: Reuse the same code across different projects.
Maintainability: Update infrastructure code in one place.
Organization: Keep Terraform code clean and structured.
Consistency: Create resources using the same configuration.

2. Real-Time Example
====================
Suppose you need to create EC2 instances for Development, Testing, and Production environments.

Without modules, you might write similar EC2 configuration multiple times.

With modules, you create the EC2 configuration once and reuse it for all three environments.
